ite47†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L156: \nL157: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2601.10305v1] DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10305v1)\nciteturn30858view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10305v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Jan 2026 (this version), latest version 25 Mar 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Hengyu Shen , cite7†Tiancheng Gu , cite8†Bin Qin , cite9†Lan Wu , cite10†Yuling Wu , cite11†Shuo Tan , cite12†Zelong Sun , cite13†Jun Wang , cite14†Nan Wu , cite15†Xiang An , cite16†Weidong Cai , cite17†Ziyong Feng , cite18†Kaicheng Yang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset, by Hengyu Shen and 12 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite19†View PDF cite20†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Vision-Language Pre-training (VLP) models demonstrate strong performance across various downstream tasks by learning from large-scale image-text pairs through contrastive pretraining. The release of extensive English image-text datasets (e.g., COYO-700M and LAION-400M) has enabled widespread adoption of models such as CLIP and SigLIP in tasks including cross-modal retrieval and image captioning.\nL17: However, the advancement of Chinese vision-language pretraining has substantially lagged behind, due to the scarcity of high-quality Chinese image-text data. To address this gap, we develop a comprehensive pipeline for constructing a high-quality Chinese cross-modal dataset. As a result, we propose DanQing, which contains 100 million image-text pairs collected from Common Crawl. Different from existing datasets, DanQing is curated through a more rigorous selection process, yielding superior data quality.\nL18: Moreover, DanQing is primarily built from 2024-2025 web data, enabling models to better capture evolving semantic trends and thus offering greater practical utility. We compare DanQing with existing datasets by continual pre-training of the SigLIP2 model. Experimental results show that DanQing consistently achieves superior performance across a range of Chinese downstream tasks, including zero-shot classification, cross-modal retrieval, and LMM-based evaluations.\nL19: To facilitate further research in Chinese vision-language pre-training, we will open-source the DanQing dataset under the Creative Common CC-BY 4.0 license.\nL20: Comments:  | 19 pages, 11 figures, 7 tables\nL21: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite21†arXiv:2601.10305 [cs.CV]\nL23:    | (or cite22†arXiv:2601.10305v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL24:    | cite23†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.10305†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Kaicheng Yang [cite24†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Thu, 15 Jan 2026 11:28:58 UTC (16,992 KB)\nL29: cite25†[v2] Fri, 30 Jan 2026 09:10:07 UTC (16,578 KB)\nL30: cite5†[v3] Wed, 25 Mar 2026 05:19:11 UTC (16,578 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled DanQing: